pact):** glibc binaries often rely on glibc-specific behaviors (symbol versions, NSS, `dlopen` paths, threading/locale internals), so on Alpine/musl they can crash, misbehave, or fail to start (e.g., `libc` symbol not found).  &#10;   **Mitigation:** rebuild or repackage the app against musl (`FROM alpine` with musl-targeted toolchain), or use an Alpine-compatible binary instead of dropping in a glibc build.&#10;&#10;2. **Security/update-risk via compatibility shims:** workarounds like `gcompat`/`libc6-compat` are partial substitutes, and you may run unsupported combinations with delayed patching and missing edge-case behavior, especially for TLS, NSS, or locale/currency/time routines.  &#10;   **Mitigation:** avoid long-term use of compatibility layers in prod; if unavoidable, isolate that service in a smaller, strictly patched image and pin/test every update path (or keep it in a glibc-based base image instead)." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="dev.alpine.llm.demo" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[101,1008][824,1979]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /></node></node><node index="5" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="dev.alpine.llm.demo" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,0][1080,283]" drawing-order="0" hint=""><node index="0" text="" resource-id="conversation_history" class="android.widget.Button" package="dev.alpine.llm.demo" content-desc="Conversation history" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="true" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[11,125][146,260]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node